 ### Neural Point Cloud Initialization from COLMAP
-A method to initialize the neural point cloud and their features for Point-NeRF using an external point cloud reconstruction (specifically COLMAP). It solves the problem of how to provide initial positions, variances, and feature vectors for the neural points. The variance parameter $\gamma_i$ for each point $p_i$ is initialized to 0.3. To acquire the feature vector $f_i$ for a point $p_i$, views where the point is occluded are ruled out, and the view where the camera is closest to the point is selected. The point is unprojected onto the feature maps extracted by the Image Feature Extraction 2D CNN (Gf) from the selected closest view to obtain $f_i$. During optimization, the confidence score of valid points is pushed to 1 [S10].
