 ### Binary Gaussian Hierarchy Construction
-The hierarchy is a binary tree. Leaf nodes contain the full set of optimized Gaussian properties (base color, SH coefficients, position, covariance). Internal nodes store merged approximations of their two child nodes [S11, unofficial].
+The hierarchy is a binary tree. Leaf nodes contain the full set of optimized Gaussian properties (base color, SH coefficients, position, covariance) [S11, unofficial]. Internal nodes store merged approximations of their two child nodes [S11, unofficial].
 
 ### Single Ellipsoid Initialization
-Initializes a single ellipsoid from a set of 3D points using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to determine orientation, center, and radii. The minimum allowed radius $r_{\min}$ is typically 0.005 to avoid numerical problems. A scaling factor $\alpha$ (typically 3) is used to ensure points are mostly covered [S12].
